brief:
  - TinyRustLM is early alpha and has never had a working release. Until the owner officially accepts a fully working release, no code debt, obsolete code or legacy support is allowed.
  - Work only in E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com on codex/model-acquisition-v2; model payloads belong only in D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM. Leave X:\LLMS alone. Keep source history in Git and preserve useful experimental lessons.
  - All 16 September reports have reviewed dispositions and applied domain guidance. Read report_decision_index before raw reports; earlier 47-report intake is historical.
  - Production Companion acquisition/conversion/inspection/transfer/listener and browser client wiring exist. There is no qualified default or proven real acquisition through that coordinator.
  - Unchanged Qwen3-0.6B@c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca stays rejected for product quality. Diagnostic numerical work does not qualify it.
  - C30 supports only current v3 registration; environment and synthetic checks passed historically, but no actual v3 registration or real trace exists. C31 canonical-input publication refactor has local regression and Edge smoke evidence; live transport capability remains blocked.
  - The owner deferred ternary/Bonsai research and requested continued implementation; no new quantizer/model research is the current task.
  - Source-authority scanning remains incomplete on two policy-blocked installer links. Do not bypass rejected deletion or describe wider cleanup as done.
  - Advance exact source quality, semantic/numerical diagnosis and real browser measurements; discover hosting capabilities alongside them. Do not replace the current format merely because a report calls it legacy.
  - MiniModel initial server seeds are authorized. Restore a usable installed model or obtain a small qualified default; keep HF/import/conversion/peer/IP controls under Advanced and prompts local.
  - Preserve distinct MemoryEndpoints agent/user lanes and local offline memory. This intake does not authorize messages or external uploads.
  - Follow .uai/next-recursive-prompt.uai and docs/ecosystem-cleanup-2026-09-12.md; commit/push coherent verified changes, with separate release and public-readback gates.
